That dictionary is 3,000 yen.

73
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:30,974
3,000 yen?

74
00:03:30,998 --> 00:03:33,080
What's that over there?

75
00:03:33,103 --> 00:03:36,397
The thing on that desk.

76
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:39,220
That's a clock.

77
00:03:39,243 --> 00:03:41,936
It's Mr. Sato's clock.

78
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:46,207
Is that clock also the school's property?

79
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:51,235
No, that's not the school's.

80
00:03:51,259 --> 00:03:53,592
It's Mr. Sato's.

81
00:03:53,615 --> 00:03:55,381
I see.

82
00:03:55,404 --> 00:03:58,581
Where is the key to this room?

83
00:03:58,605 --> 00:04:01,844
The room key is here.

84
00:04:01,868 --> 00:04:04,148
It's inside the desk.

85
00:04:04,172 --> 00:04:06,538
Got it.

86
00:04:06,561 --> 00:04:08,695
Thank you.

87
00:04:08,718 --> 00:04:17,263
If you understood, please leave a comment!

88
00:04:17,263 --> 00:04:20,263
Scene 3: Navigating the Station and Buying Tickets

89
00:04:20,263 --> 00:04:21,917
Excuse me.

90
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:24,794
Where is the station restroom?

91
00:04:24,818 --> 00:04:28,106
The restroom is over there.

92
00:04:28,130 --> 00:04:30,896
It's next to the kiosk.

93
00:04:30,919 --> 00:04:32,930
Over there, right?

94
00:04:32,954 --> 00:04:35,287
Thank you.

95
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:38,477
Where is the ticket counter?

96
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:42,079
The ticket counter is here.

97
00:04:42,103 --> 00:04:44,281
This window.

98
00:04:44,304 --> 00:04:46,671
Here?

99
00:04:46,694 --> 00:04:50,060
How much is a ticket to Tokyo?

100
00:04:50,083 --> 00:04:53,850
A ticket to Tokyo is 160 yen.

101
00:04:53,873 --> 00:04:57,406
160 yen?

102
00:04:57,429 --> 00:05:01,196
Is Mr. Suzuki's ticket 160 yen too?

103
00:05:01,219 --> 00:05:06,598
No, my ticket isn't 160 yen.

104
00:05:06,621 --> 00:05:09,188
It's 190 yen.

105
00:05:09,211 --> 00:05:11,144
I see.

106
00:05:11,167 --> 00:05:14,051
Where is the information desk?

107
00:05:14,075 --> 00:05:16,875
The information desk is that way.

108
00:05:16,898 --> 00:05:19,745
Next to the south exit.

109
00:05:19,768 --> 00:05:22,041
That way, right?

110
00:05:22,065 --> 00:05:25,081
What's that building over there?

111
00:05:25,104 --> 00:05:28,386
That's a station hotel.

112
00:05:28,410 --> 00:05:33,143
Is that hotel owned by a Japanese company?

113
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:37,566
Yes, it's a Japanese company's hotel.

114
00:05:37,589 --> 00:05:40,522
Where is your company, Mr. Suzuki?

115
00:05:40,545 --> 00:05:43,779
My company is here.

116
00:05:43,802 --> 00:05:45,768
We're inside the station.

117
00:05:45,791 --> 00:05:48,438
Inside the station?

118
00:05:48,462 --> 00:05:50,462
How convenient!

119
00:05:50,485 --> 00:05:54,091
Yes, it's very convenient.

120
00:05:54,115 --> 00:05:57,081
Where is your school, Tanaka?

121
00:05:57,104 --> 00:06:00,038
My school is over there.

122
00:06:00,061 --> 00:06:03,479
It's on the third floor of that building.

123
00:06:03,502 --> 00:06:05,998
Oh, that building, right?

124
00:06:06,021 --> 00:06:08,421
Yes, that's right.

125
00:06:08,444 --> 00:06:11,444
Scene 4: Meeting and Work Schedule

126
00:06:11,444 --> 00:06:16,778
Suzuki, what time does tomorrow's meeting start?

127
00:06:16,801 --> 00:06:22,267
Tomorrow's meeting is from 10 AM to 12 PM.

128
00:06:22,290 --> 00:06:24,372
Starting at 10 AM, got it.

129
00:06:24,396 --> 00:06:26,997
Where is it being held?

130
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:30,786
The meeting room is on the third floor.

131
00:06:30,809 --> 00:06:35,043
There are plenty of documents on the table.

132
00:06:35,066 --> 00:06:36,755
Thank you.

133
00:06:36,778 --> 00:06:40,464
Do you have work this afternoon?

134
00:06:40,488 --> 00:06:46,154
Yes, I’ll be working from 1 PM to 5 PM today.

135
00:06:46,177 --> 00:06:51,511
How many hours do you work every day?

136
00:06:51,534 --> 00:06:54,667
I work eight hours every day.

137
00:06:54,690 --> 00:06:59,123
Tanaka, what time did you work until yesterday?

138
00:06:59,147 --> 00:07:03,834
I worked until 9 PM last night.

139
00:07:03,857 --> 00:07:06,277
Until 9 PM?

140
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,379
That must have been tough.

141
00:07:08,403 --> 00:07:13,403
Yeah, but I’m not working tonight.

142
00:07:13,426 --> 00:07:16,633
You have the night off?

143
00:07:16,656 --> 00:07:19,889
Yes, I do.

144
00:07:19,912 --> 00:07:25,205
Suzuki, would you like to grab dinner together tonight?

145
00:07:25,229 --> 00:07:27,029
Sounds great!

146
00:07:27,052 --> 00:07:29,462
Where should we eat?

147
00:07:29,486 --> 00:07:32,886
Let’s eat at the restaurant in front of the station.

148
00:07:32,909 --> 00:07:35,743
What time should we go to the restaurant?

149
00:07:35,767 --> 00:07:38,200
Let’s go at 7 PM.

150
00:07:38,223 --> 00:07:40,708
Are we going by car?

151
00:07:40,731 --> 00:07:43,665
No, we’ll take the train.

152
00:07:43,688 --> 00:07:45,526
Got it.

153
00:07:45,549 --> 00:07:49,282
Alright, see you in front of the restaurant at 7 PM.

154
00:07:49,305 --> 00:07:51,958
Yes, see you tonight.

155
00:07:51,981 --> 00:07:54,981
